# Routes Helix / DA.live / Config Service work to the skill with the auth+scoping rules.
#
# These three APIs share a property that makes guessing expensive: they RETURN
# SUCCESS for writes that did not take effect. Every mutation in this feature is
# confirmed by a re-read for that reason.
rule_id=eds-publish
rule_once=1

rule_match() {
    case "$1" in
        Edit|Write) ;;
        *) return 1 ;;
    esac
    [ -n "$3" ] || return 1
    case "$3" in
        */eds/services/helix/*) return 0 ;;
        */eds/services/daLive/*) return 0 ;;
        */eds/services/configService/*) return 0 ;;
    esac
    return 1
}

rule_message() {
    cat <<'MSG'
You are editing a Helix / DA.live / Config Service path. Invoke the
`eds-publish-and-config` skill (Skill tool, skill: "eds-publish-and-config") first.

These APIs return SUCCESS for writes that did not take effect, which is why every
mutation here is confirmed by a re-read rather than by the write's own status. The
skill carries the auth and scoping rules that are not guessable:

  - which token each operation needs — a DELETE /live 403 "while source exists" is
    checked against fstab.yaml and ONLY the DA.live IMS bearer token bypasses it
  - site config vs org config: `aem.repositoryId` must be written to the SITE
    config or the block library appears and AEM Assets does not
  - `grantSiteAdmin` REPLACES the role list; use ensureSiteAdmin/revokeSiteAdmin

This hook fires only once per session.
MSG
}
